pit. My con was about 12 I believe and str was mediocre as well.  I 
started as a dwarf with low con so I decided to do a pure racket. I 
normally don't do that anymore but I wanted to keep the game 
exciting. 

First order of business was to relax while my pet got some exp. I ate 
two rations while Mr dog went around killing stuff. Then I went down. 
The fork to the mines came up on level two, but I ignored it. I 
didn't have enough gold. 

There was a armor shop on level three so I exchanged my fedora and 
leather jacket for some dwarven chain and head gear. I lovingly 
folded my jacket in the corner and hung up the hat in a nice dry 
place. Me and the dog then conned the shopkeeper of all his gold.  I 
had 1600 gold at this point. I could have gone to minetown at this 
point but that would have been asking for it. I did go into the first 
level of the mines to get more armor. 

On level 5 there was a huge potion shop. I priced id'ed all the 
potions. Any 200 I dipped junk in. All 50 range had darts dipped in 
them. I identified sickness, healing and extra healing. (amound 
others) I don't think there was an altar so I drank them as they 
where.  Now I had enough to go to minetown, but I found the oracle on 
the level below. Since sokobon was so close I went there instead. 

Lvl 7 had a small general store in addition to the entrance to 
sokobon. I tamed about 6 pets in sokobon but it was too much for 
them. I came out with only two. At this point I had about 6600 gold 
and around 30 something hps. My con had gone up to around 15 so I was 
starting to feel pretty good. I had enough gold and lawfuls can do 
the mines easier. Sokobon yielded a BoH.

I made it to minetown very easily this time. No bones files to mess 
